## SECTION 3

3.a. What does **cloning** the repo mean?

```
   Cloning a repo means making your own copy of the repository
   from GitHub onto your computer
```

- What is the **repository**? Where does it exist (on your local machine or in Github)?

```
    A repository is basically where all the code and files for the project are stored.
    The main repo is on GitHub, and when I clone it, I get my own copy on my computer.
```

- What is a **commit**? Why does it need a commit message?

```
    A commit is basically saving the changes I made to my code.
    It needs a message so I know what changes I made in that commit.

```

- What does it mean to **push** your code? Where is your code being pushed _to_ and _from_?

```
Pushing means sending the changes from my computer to the repository on
GitHub so they are saved there.

```

